# PMTwin Architecture Resolution

## Project Context

- B2B marketplace connecting Project Managers, consultants, and companies in Saudi Arabia
- Current state: Sophisticated browser-based POC with business logic in localStorage-backed JavaScript
- Target: SaaS-ready platform serving 100,000+ concurrent users
- Architecture authority chain: Domain Blueprint → Command Architecture → Unified Lifecycle Engine → This sprint

## Critical Constraints

1. NEVER implement backend logic in POC/ folder — POC is legacy runtime only
2. NEVER import TypeScript from web/ into POC/ or JavaScript from POC/ into web/
3. ALL lifecycle state names MUST come from @pm-twin/lifecycle registry (manifest.json)
4. NO direct localStorage mutations outside of data-service.js (to be replaced in Phase 2)
5. ALL new code must pass: lint → type-check → unit test → build

## File Authority Matrix

| Path | Authority | Can Import From |
|------|-----------|-----------------|
| packages/lifecycle/ | SOURCE OF TRUTH | Nothing (zero-dependency) |
| web/src/ | Consumer | packages/lifecycle/, node_modules |
| POC/src/ | Legacy (read-only Phase 1) | packages/lifecycle/ (static serve only) |
| docs/adr/ | Immutable after approval | Nothing |
